UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The King of Swords represents the absolute archetype of "Systemic Governance"—the apex of the air element where the sovereign consciousness has fully matured into a legislative, long-term architect of its own, logical manifest reality. Moving beyond the discerning presence of the Queen, the King signifies the stage of "The Sovereign Lawgiver," where your analytical power is no longer merely a lens you inhabit, but a structured, justice-administering instrument you actively command. Visually depicted as a king seated on a throne, holding a sword firmly and upright, this archetype embodies the concept of "Sovereign Authority"—the realization that true power is the ability to leverage your mental clarity to establish, maintain, and uphold a framework that serves the greater, objective order of your life. Within the complex architecture of your psyche, this is the stage of "Strategic Legislation," where your perceptions, your ethics, and your decisions have harmonized into a coherent, enduring, and authoritative blueprint for existence. When the King of Swords appears, your system is registering a "Maximum Sovereign" status; you are the undisputed lawgiver of your domain, and you are being invited to take full responsibility for the architecture of your logic. This card commands you to perform a brutal audit of your principles. You are being tasked with the essential work of "Intentional Legislation": moving past the need for external validation or temporary opinion, and dedicating your focus to the construction of a foundation that will stand the test of time. To inhabit the King of Swords is to master the art of "Sovereign Justice," recognizing that by directing your intellectual sword with the cold, clear eye of a master, you are effectively transforming your life from a series of reactive arguments into a deliberate, intentional, and sovereign work of logic.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the King of Swords appears in the reversed position, it acts as a high-intensity signal of "Systemic Autocracy," "Legislative-Collapse," or the catastrophic—yet curative—failure to manage the intellectual power you have claimed, leading to a state of aggressive, rigid, and fundamentally unstable dogmatism. The reversal suggests that you are currently running a high-priority, high-cost maintenance script that equates "uncompromising enforcement" with "true leadership," even as your internal operating system is experiencing a critical, ego-driven fracture of its original commitment to truth. You are essentially "legislating for a failing state," running a protocol that prioritizes the ego’s desire to "never be questioned" over the sober, unglamorous requirement to actually serve the justice you once claimed to protect. This creates a massive, systemic misalignment: you are intellectually and behaviorally attempting to perform the role of the "infallible judge," while internally, you are being hollowed out by a profound, gnawing sense of isolation, leading to a state of chronic, high-latency irritability, the experience of "ruling over a fractured consensus," and a persistent, gnawing awareness that your "authority" is built upon the silencing of dissent rather than the power of sound reason. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking your life force into a "feedback loop of ego-validation"; you are obsessively trying to force your logical framework upon the environment, refusing to accept that the only thing keeping you from the necessary, final dismantling of your tyranny is your own, deep-seated fear that without the power to command, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, hollow state. The reversed King of Swords exposes the hidden, egoic fear that drives this behavior: the paralyzing terror of loss of intellectual control, and the corresponding fear that if you were to drop the pretense of the "mighty lawgiver" and return to the silence of your own, unvalidated work, you would be forced to face the reality of your own, present-day, unanchored self. This reversal commands an immediate, radical intervention: you must stop the output of these authoritarian, control-seeking scripts, perform a brutal audit of your legislative style, and confront the reality of why you were so hesitant to prioritize the integrity of your principles over the comfort of your command. It is a demand to stop the self-deception that keeps you tethered to a state of chronic, high-maintenance dissonance, and to initiate the move toward a genuine, humble, and often terrifying reclamation of your own, individual authority. You are being tasked with the uncomfortable, yet essential, work of radical decentralization—accepting that the "stuckness" you feel is the direct result of having prioritized the comfort of "ruling" over the vulnerability of "serving," and realizing that until you are willing to let the throne crumble and stand in the raw, unadorned reality of your own, honest truth, you will continue to be starved by the very, phantom authority you have worked so hard to simulate.'
WHERE id = 42;
